{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LzsjCHR9mcXa4J1uNhq8RA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NASA Voyager 2 at Uranus \"closest approach\" 17:59 EST Jan. 24, 1986 Miranda 17,560 miles Challenger\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Voyager Mission Description - Ring-Moon Systems Node Home\",\"url\":\"<redacted> Uranus Science Summary\",\"url\":\"<redacted> (moon)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miranda_(moon)\"},{\"title\":\"Voyager Celebrates 25 Years Since Uranus Visit | NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL)\",\"url\":\"<redacted> 2\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyager_2\"},{\"title\":\"List of missions to the outer planets\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_missions_to_the_outer_planets\"},{\"title\":\"Voyager 2 met Uranus 40 years ago\",\"url\":\"<redacted> Years After Uranus Flyby, Voyager 2 Sails On | Space\",\"url\":\"<redacted> Satellite - Miranda | NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL)\",\"url\":\"<redacted> at Uranus - NASA Science\",\"url\":\"<redacted> on the search results, here's what I found regarding NASA's Voyager 2 encounter with Uranus:\n\nThe Voyager 2 closest approach to Uranus was on 24 January 1986 at 17:59 UTC at a distance of 107000 km from the center of Uranus. (Note: The search result specifies this time as 17:59 UTC, which is equivalent to 12:59 EST, not 17:59 EST as mentioned in your query.)\n\nAt its closest, the spacecraft came within 81,500 kilometers (50,600 miles) of Uranus's cloud tops on January 24, 1986.\n\nRegarding Miranda, Miranda's closest approach distance was 29,000 km on 24 Jan according to the NASA source data, which differs from the 17,560 miles (approximately 28,265 km) mentioned in your query.\n\nOn Jan. 24, 1986 — just four days before the space shuttle Challenger exploded during liftoff, killing all seven astronauts aboard — NASA's robotic Voyager 2 probe zoomed by Uranus, the seventh planet from the sun.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8e00c32-ad4c-4f87-9816-63ab7901b1e1","uuid":"765a3e2c-a225-4bfe-98bd-fc7dcd2e19e7","timestamp":"2026-09-26T17:07:28.200Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"NASA Voyager 2 at Uranus \"closest approach\" 17:59 EST Jan. 24, 1986 Miranda 17,560 miles Challenger","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BjFTgPFqoRn9Vc6vsnXhoy","content":[{"title":"Voyager Mission Description - Ring-Moon Systems Node Home","url":"<redacted> Uranus Science Summary","url":"<redacted> (moon)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miranda_(moon)"},{"title":"Voyager Celebrates 25 Years Since Uranus Visit | NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL)","url":"<redacted> 2","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyager_2"},{"title":"List of missions to the outer planets","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_missions_to_the_outer_planets"},{"title":"Voyager 2 met Uranus 40 years ago","url":"<redacted> Years After Uranus Flyby, Voyager 2 Sails On | Space","url":"<redacted> Satellite - Miranda | NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL)","url":"<redacted> at Uranus - NASA Science","url":"<redacted> on the search results, here's what I found regarding NASA's Voyager 2 encounter with Uranus:\n\nThe Voyager 2 closest approach to Uranus was on 24 January 1986 at 17:59 UTC at a distance of 107000 km from the center of Uranus. (Note: The search result specifies this time as 17:59 UTC, which is equivalent to 12:59 EST, not 17:59 EST as mentioned in your query.)\n\nAt its closest, the spacecraft came within 81,500 kilometers (50,600 miles) of Uranus's cloud tops on January 24, 1986.\n\nRegarding Miranda, Miranda's closest approach distance was 29,000 km on 24 Jan according to the NASA source data, which differs from the 17,560 miles (approximately 28,265 km) mentioned in your query.\n\nOn Jan. 24, 1986 — just four days before the space shuttle Challenger exploded during liftoff, killing all seven astronauts aboard — NASA's robotic Voyager 2 probe zoomed by Uranus, the seventh planet from the sun."],"durationSeconds":5.311885056000001,"searchCount":1}}
